Here's a simple HTML website that displays a random joke from a list of 4 jokes when a user clicks a button.

### ✅ Features:
- A button that the user can click.
- When clicked, it shows a random joke from a predefined list.

---

### 📄 `index.html`

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Random Joke Generator</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            text-align: center;
            padding-top: 100px;
        }
        button {
            padding: 10px 20px;
            font-size: 16px;
            cursor: pointer;
        }
        #joke {
            margin-top: 30px;
            font-size: 18px;
            color: #333;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>Random Joke Generator</h1>
    <button onclick="showRandomJoke()">Tell Me a Joke</button>
    <div id="joke"></div>

    <script>
        const jokes = [
            "Why don't scientists trust atoms? Because they make up everything!",
            "What do you call fake spaghetti? An impasta!",
            "Why did the scarecrow win an award? Because he was outstanding in his field!",
            "What do you get when you cross a snowman and a vampire? Frostbite!"
        ];

        function showRandomJoke() {
            const randomIndex = Math.floor(Math.random() * jokes.length);
            document.getElementById("joke").textContent = jokes[randomIndex];
        }
    </script>

</body>
</html>
```

---

### 📌 How to Use:
1. Save the code above in a file named `index.html`.
2. Open it in any web browser.
3. Click the **"Tell Me a Joke"** button to see a random joke from the list.

